Omarchy shell modules, vendored for the niri port
=================================================

These files come from the Omarchy shell (https://github.com/omacom/omarchy,
branch `quattro`, path `shell/Commons` and `shell/Ui`). Omarchy is MIT
licensed; see LICENSE beside this notice.

Flea vendors only the modules its QML imports, instead of symlinking
`/usr/share/omarchy/shell`:

  Commons/Color.qml
  Commons/Style.qml
  Commons/Util.qml
  Commons/Border.qml
  Commons/BorderGeometry.js
  Commons/qmldir
  Ui/BorderSurface.qml
  Ui/BorderOverlay.qml
  Ui/PanelSectionHeader.qml
  Ui/PanelSeparator.qml
  Ui/qmldir

The qmldir files list only the vendored entries, so an undeclared Omarchy
type cannot be resolved by accident.

Local patches, kept minimal so a future rebase is a diff and not a rewrite:

  Commons/Color.qml
    - `currentThemePath` reads `$XDG_STATE_HOME/flea/theme`, with
      `FLEA_THEME_DIR` as an override, instead of the Omarchy state path.
    - `userShellFile` reads `~/.config/flea/shell.toml`, not
      `~/.config/omarchy/shell.toml`.
    - `loadColors` honours an explicit `urgent` key before falling back to
      `red`/`color1`, so Noctalia's `colors.error` is the urgent colour.

  Commons/Style.qml
    - `cornerRadius` defaults to 10 (or `FLEA_CORNER_RADIUS`) under niri,
      where `hyprctl` cannot answer.
    - `refresh()` only queries `hyprctl` when a Hyprland instance exists.
    - The `Quickshell.Hyprland` import and the config-reload connection are
      removed; niri has no equivalent event and Flea keeps the niri default.

Everything else is unmodified Omarchy code.
